{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftNLP\/documentation\/SwiftNLP"]]},"kind":"article","topicSections":[{"title":"WordNet Types","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftNLP\/documentation\/SwiftNLP\/WordNet","doc:\/\/SwiftNLP\/documentation\/SwiftNLP\/Synset","doc:\/\/SwiftNLP\/documentation\/SwiftNLP\/POS"],"anchor":"WordNet-Types"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiftNLP\/documentation\/SwiftNLP\/WordNetAndLexicalGraphs","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"role":"collectionGroup","title":"WordNet Semantic Hierarchy & Lexical Graphs","modules":[{"name":"SwiftNLP"}],"roleHeading":"API Collection"},"abstract":[{"text":"Navigate semantic relationships, compute synset distances, and explore English hypernym\/hyponym trees.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"WordNet","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a large lexical database of English where nouns, verbs, adjectives, and adverbs are organized into sets of cognitive synonyms called ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Synsets","type":"text"}]},{"text":", interlinked by conceptual-semantic and lexical relations.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"1. Looking Up Synsets & Definitions","anchor":"1-Looking-Up-Synsets--Definitions","level":2},{"type":"codeListing","code":["import SwiftNLP","","let wordnet = WordNet.shared","","\/\/ Look up all noun synsets for \"bank\"","let synsets = wordnet.synsets(for: \"bank\", pos: .noun)","for s in synsets {","    print(\"ID: \\(s.id), Definition: \\(s.definition)\")","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","text":"2. Semantic Similarity Metrics","anchor":"2-Semantic-Similarity-Metrics","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"SwiftSci implements standard lexical similarity algorithms:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"t